[
{"claim": "The mind tab (2026-08-16): the agent apps fourth tab - status/statistics/tools/configuration for the autonomous machinery. UI lives in agent.chat control facets, edited ONLY via dev-code-read_control_facet + patch_control_facet (nn_sessionid is a required param; pass empty). The HTTP exec envelope nests the command result under .data ({status,pid,nn_return_type,data}) - unwrap before reading fields; the top-level pid is the EXECUTION id, not a process. Backend: agent-model train_status (train.pid + log tail), get_settings/set_setting (live globals + botd.properties rewrite, secret keys masked/refused), promote_pointer (POST /promote client). Verified in headless Chromium against a disposable running the real server.", "tags": "ui", "confidence": "high", "time": 1786899133189},
{"claim": "The chat pane has a sessions sidebar (2026-08-25): switch between or start conversations without losing the current one, all browser-local.", "detail": "Landed as journaled facet patches p50-p55 on agent.chat. Storage: an index at localStorage key agent.chat.sessions.v1 plus one record per session at agent.chat.s.<id>, each capped at 60 messages / 120 cells (the old single-session cap). Every message persists to its session record as it happens, so switching saves nothing and loads both rendered cells and model context. New sessions are not listed until their first message; the old agent.chat.v1 single-session key auto-migrates into the first sidebar entry on first load. Session titles come from the first user message and shift if early messages age out of the cap. Memory, journals, and the archivist queue are untouched.", "tags": "agent.chat,sessions,sidebar,localStorage,ui,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1787660334918},
{"claim": "The chat supports attachments (2026-08-25): 📎 button, drag & drop onto the chat, and paste-screenshot; files save via agent.chat.upload to runtime/agent/uploads/ and the outgoing message gains an [ATTACHED FILES] block of absolute paths, with text files ≤32KB inlined.", "detail": "Landed as journaled patches p56-p59 on agent.chat plus the upload command (hand-rolled base64 decoder, sanitized basename, 20MB client cap). Transport: uploads go as a JSON POST to ../app/exec with sessionid in the querystring, NOT through invokeCommand — that path rides the websocket or GET/JSONP and cannot carry megabytes. Multipart POST was rejected on purpose: app/service/init.rs deletes the per-request temp dir immediately after parsing the parts, before command execution, so tempfile params (write_asset's contract) point at already-deleted files. The model is text-only across every chat_llm arm, so images are not seen as pixels; the agent opens saved paths with its tools.", "tags": "agent.chat,attachments,upload,transport", "confidence": "high", "time": 1787665116676},
{"claim": "The agent chat prepends a hidden context preamble as its own user message ([CONTEXT] + the memory:index fence) ahead of the user's real first question - any consumer that reads 'the first user message' (session titling did) gets the preamble, not the question.", "detail": "Bit the history sidebar: sessTitle() titled every saved session '[CONTEXT] ```memory:index ...'. Fixed 2026-08-25 in agent.chat js (patches p63/p64): title generation skips user messages starting with [CONTEXT], plus a one-time load repair retitling saved sessions from their stored messages. Rule going forward: anything scanning a session's messages for the user's words must skip [CONTEXT]-prefixed user turns.", "tags": "agent.chat,context-injection,session-titles,gotcha,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1787681286562},
{"claim": "The plan tab (2026-08-25): a kanban board over kb.plan, in the new agent.plan control mounted as agent.chat's fifth tab via two html patches (the generic tab switcher needed no js/css changes).", "detail": "Backend: agent-plan-board reads kb.plan's memory facet and returns entries plus the facet content hash; agent-plan-move_item swaps the lifecycle token in an entry's tags (preserving other tags/fields) and writes the whole facet through the journaled dev.code.patch_control_facet with the board hash as concurrency token - stale kb.plan answers err stale_base and the UI reloads; agent-plan-add_item files new items via agent.archivist.remember as plan,proposed, confidence medium, author from the calling session. UI: five columns matching the lifecycle tokens epistemic_work derives from (proposed/accepted/in-progress/done/abandoned), drag-to-move, entries lacking a lifecycle token surface in proposed and normalize on first move. Verified live: a roundtrip move landed as kb.plan journal patches. New commands default admin-only.", "tags": "agent.plan,agent.chat,kb.plan,kanban,ui,lifecycle,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1787685134242},
{"claim": "installControl never rewrites a declared data-control attribute, so a sibling lookup must match the declaration string exactly: work_udo declared data-control='agent:stage:{}' but selected [data-control=\"agent:stage\"], got null, and the chat's ready threw before wiring the ask form - with no console error, the form fell back to a native submit that just reloads the page. Declare helper mounts bare (data-control=\"agent:stage\") and read optional ones with ?.api. A chat that 'does nothing' on ask is this failure class.", "tags": "chat,debugging", "confidence": "high", "time": 1792244525790, "sources": [{"lib": "agent", "ctl": "chat", "facet": "js"}]},
{"claim": "The chat pane has user-draggable resize dividers (2026-10-26): .ag-sdiv between the sessions sidebar and the chat column (width), and .ag-adiv between the thread and the message box (textarea height), both localStorage-persisted with double-click reset — pure agent.chat facet edits, no compile.", "detail": "Placement lesson from the session: each handle must be a direct flex child of the container whose axis it divides — dropped inside .ag-chat-main (a column flex), the 6px-wide sidebar handle collapsed to 0px tall, invisible and unclickable with no error. The handles straddle existing 1px borders via negative margins (-3px) with z-index 1 so the neighbor doesn't steal the pointer. Message-box drag sets an inline height on .ag-input clamped between 52px and whatever leaves the thread 120px; keys agent.chat.sidebarw/agent.chat.inputh in localStorage.", "tags": "agent.chat,ui,resize,facets,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1793017217692},
{"claim": "The Mind tab in agent.chat is a sectioned settings workspace (mind-tab-redesign branch, 2026-10-28): six sidebar sections (conversation, activity, learning, personality, insights, advanced) built by mindBuild() from template[data-mt] elements in the html facet, with a draft→Review→Apply model for settings/rates/persona and instant data-live switches for executive/sensor/plan autonomy and per-repo commits.", "detail": "Pieces: html facet = .mx workspace shell (heading with Show-config-keys toggle, .mx-side nav, .mx-panes, .mx-review, .mx-foot footer) plus six <template data-mt=...> sections; js mind block runs from the '── the mind tab' comment through mApply() — mindBuild/renderRepos/renderCfg/mBindValues/mindRefresh/loadMind (5s poll, baselines from get_settings + executive drive, never overwrites drafted or focused fields) and mChangesList/mErrors/mShowReview/mApply (sequential apply, persona last, failures stay in the draft). Every control calls the same platform command the old card grid called, with the same params. Implemented per ~/Desktop/mind-tab-redesign/mind-tab-spec.md; commit f63c146, not merged, not pushed.", "tags": "agent.chat,mind-tab,frontend", "source": {"lib": "agent", "ctl": "chat", "facet": "js", "hash": "f4db2c86d9279b10"}, "confidence": "high", "time": 1793189241596},
{"claim": "The .ag-chip CSS rules in agent.chat's css facet are SHARED: the chat pane's attachment chips render with the mind block's .ag-chip rules (loaded later, they win the shared properties), so any mind-tab restyle must keep those five .ag-chip rules verbatim; all other mind CSS is scoped under [data-pane=\"mind\"] or .mx-* classes.", "detail": "Confirmed during the 2026-10-28 mind-tab redesign: the attachment chip base rule near the chat block sets inline-flex/8px radius, but the mind block's .ag-chip (inline-block, 999px radius, .ok/.warn/.err/.off variants) overrides it. The redesign kept them verbatim under a comment in the '── the mind tab' CSS section; the new mind pane uses the separate .chip class instead.", "tags": "agent.chat,css,mind-tab,hazard", "source": {"lib": "agent", "ctl": "chat", "facet": "css", "hash": "d2a0d5af97f3ae3b"}, "confidence": "high", "time": 1793189249018},
{"claim": "The Mind tab's footer became a hidden unsaved-changes bar (2026-10-28 spec update, §2 items 2 and 4): .mx-foot is absolutely positioned over the pane bottom, slides in (180ms transform+opacity, .show class + inert toggle via mBarSync) when the draft first gains a change, slides away when it empties, and stays hidden while the Review/result screen is open; .mx-content gets .padbar bottom padding while it shows.", "detail": "mBarSync(count) replaced mToast — the apply toast is gone because the result screen is the confirmation; Discard/Review buttons are always enabled (the bar only exists with pending changes). Same update added [data-pane=\"mind\"] button:disabled { opacity:.45; cursor:default } with :hover pins (line for plain buttons, accent for .primary) so disabled buttons show no hover border change, and gave every sidebar status dot its meaning as title + aria-label (mDotTips, computed beside mDots in loadMind; the conversation tip reuses the hoisted armName provider label). Commit 02ff5fa on mind-tab-redesign.", "tags": "agent.chat,mind-tab,frontend", "confidence": "high", "time": 1793193860870},
{"claim": "The global .ag-app button:hover border rule still fires on disabled buttons, so disabled styling needs explicit :hover pins per pane", "detail": "CSS :hover matches disabled form controls, so the app-wide .ag-app button:hover border change makes disabled buttons look active. The mind pane fix (02ff5fa) pairs [data-pane=\"mind\"] button:disabled { opacity:.45; cursor:default; } with two :hover pins (--line for plain buttons, --accent for .primary) to keep the global rule from firing. Any other pane styling disabled buttons in the agent app needs the same pinning.", "tags": "agent.chat,css,frontend,mind-tab,unreviewed", "confidence": "medium", "time": 1793195026219},
{"claim": "Overlapping persist() calls that save a record with a null id each mint a separate record — agent.chat now serializes every session save on one promise chain to kill this double-id-mint race.", "detail": "app.write with a null id mints a new id per call, so two unawaited saves racing before the first id lands create two session records. Any unawaited save path that relies on null-id minting has this race; the fix pattern is chaining all saves on a single promise rather than firing them independently. Landed in chat-save-fix Phase 1 (commit 518dc91) alongside the pre-turn save.", "tags": "agent.chat,app.app,save,race,app.write,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1793427164838},
{"claim": "agent.chat's js facet is a strict-mode ES module with top-level const helpers declared mid-file, so code patched in above their declarations hits the temporal dead zone.", "detail": "Bit during the chat-save work: a patch redeclared chatMain (a const defined further down for drag-drop), and the lsGet/lsSet/lsDel localStorage helpers are declared BELOW the on-load restore point, so earlier code cannot call them (TDZ, module strict mode). Safe patterns: scope new bindings locally inside the inserted functions, or use self-contained accessors instead of the facet's own helpers.", "tags": "agent.chat,js-facet,strict-mode,tdz,patch-gotcha,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1793455958660},
{"claim": "The agent chat's websocket auth reads the bare global `sessionid`; adopting a fresh session id must assign window.sessionid (bare assignment throws in the strict-mode module), and that one write covers both transports.", "detail": "Both json() and invokeCommand read the global sessionid, so after recovering a session over HTTP (cookie session via fetch credentials:same-origin), writing window.sessionid fixes websocket and HTTP calls alike. Only adopt when the cookie session belongs to the same signed-in user.", "tags": "agent.chat,sessionid,websocket,auth,strict-mode,unreviewed", "confidence": "high", "time": 1793455965141},
{"claim": "Sessions die of request silence, not transport: every authenticated request over either transport (HTTP-with-cookie or websocket frame) refreshes a session's last_contact, so a long in-flight command like an LLM turn that sends nothing for sessiontimeoutmillis kills its own session. The HTTP ?sessionid= query param is silently ignored (the cookie always wins); websocket frames honor the page's sessionid variable; and GET /app/login with the same cookie revives the SAME session id.", "detail": "Proved on a 60s-timeout scratch rig (chat-save-fix Phase 0, 2026-10-31; runtime/qa/agent-chat-save/): 30s polls on either transport kept a session alive for minutes while an idle control session expired at ~150s. current_user?sessionid=<valid> with no cookie answers Anonymous, and with both present a bogus cookie beats a valid param - so api.js's HTTP fallback only works when the cookie happens to match, and a save can only be routed past a clobbered cookie via the websocket. Re-login re-binds the signed-in user to the cookie's existing id, so a page's stored sessionid becomes valid again after a re-login in any tab. This is why agent.chat saves over the websocket and pings current_user every 60s only while a turn runs.", "tags": "agent.chat,sessions,auth,websocket,cookie,platform", "source": {"lib": "agent", "ctl": "chat", "facet": "js", "hash": "e8a6a0429f49d444"}, "confidence": "high", "time": 1793475727929},
{"claim": "agent.chat's save pipeline (chat-save-fix, 2026-10-31): persist() writes over the websocket (cookie-fetch fallback), serialized on one saveChain; the user's message is saved before chatTurn starts; a 60s current_user keepalive runs only while a turn is in flight (window.__agKeepaliveMs overrides it for tests); busy cells are never persisted and a trailing saved one renders 'This reply wasn't saved.'; any non-ok save shows a recoverable banner plus a send guard; a localStorage backup (agent.chat.unsaved.<username>) restores on load when newer than the store record; and a refused session_index leaves the existing sidebar rows in place instead of blanking them.", "detail": "Commits 518dc91..cc626d1 on the js facet. Recovery: on focus/visibilitychange or every 30s while the banner shows, re-check current_user, adopt the cookie's sessionid into window.sessionid only when it is the same signed-in user, retry the save, and delete the backup for that sessId on success. The send guard blocks chat_llm when the last save failed or current_user has no groups, keeping the typed text in the input so no reply can be lost to a dead session. 5MB+ sessions round-trip intact over the websocket (QA C14), so no size fallback was needed. Full QA: runtime/qa/agent-chat-save/REPORT.md (C01-C17, all pass).", "tags": "agent.chat,save,persistence,keepalive,recovery,backup", "source": {"lib": "agent", "ctl": "chat", "facet": "js", "hash": "e8a6a0429f49d444"}, "confidence": "high", "time": 1793475737004},
{"end": true}]
